-- Q6194: Misstatements and Control Deficiencies [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 450.06, factual misstatements are those about which there is no doubt, typically identified in items tested 100%. Projected misstatements arise from extrapolating sample results to the population. The $45,000 error found in a complete examination is factual, while the $22,000 sample error requires projection under AU-C 530.
Wrong (A): Not both are projected; the $45,000 error was found through 100% examination and requires no projection since the entire subpopulation was tested.
Wrong (B): While both have specific dollar amounts, the $22,000 sample error must be extrapolated to the untested population rather than treated as a factual misstatement.
Wrong (D): The $22,000 error is a projected misstatement from sampling, not a judgmental misstatement; judgmental misstatements involve differences in estimates or accounting policy selections.$EXPL$
